.TH ANONIFY-BROWSER 1 "2026-11-06" "anonify 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anonify-browser \- open Firefox or LibreWolf with a throwaway, hardened profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anonify-browser
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B anonify-browser
starts a browser with a freshly created profile in RAM, hardened preferences
and a sanitized environment, then removes the profile when the browser exits.
It never touches the user's normal profile, history or bookmarks, and it does
not need root.
.PP
The helper works on Linux, Windows and macOS; the rest of
.B anonify
is Linux-only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-lang \fR(\fIen\fR|\fIes\fR)
Force a message language instead of detecting it from the OS locale.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I URL
Page to open. Only http and https are accepted. Omit it for a blank start.
.SH BROWSER SELECTION
The first of
.BR librewolf ", " firefox ", " firefox-esr
found in
.B PATH
is used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, non-zero when no supported browser is installed or the
browser cannot be started.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR anonify (1)
